{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit `sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 2.5);` prior before `sigma_y` is used in the likelihood. This matches the finite bounded support already declared for `sigma_y` and satisfies SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before use. The data are unchanged. `N`, `J`, and `movie` are context inputs, not protected observations.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] y;
  int J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> movie;
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=5>[J] theta;
  real<lower=0, upper=2.5> sigma_y;
}
model {
  theta ~ normal(3, 1);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 2.5);
  y ~ normal(theta[movie], sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":5,"N":2,"movie":[2,2],"y":[2.0,2.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
